Vendored airunner_common (issue #2243, Gap 1)
============================================

What
----
`airunner_common/` is a byte-verified copy of the 13 pure-Python modules from
the airunner-common 6.1.8 wheel (no dist-info), included in the frozen CORE
runtime by the PyInstaller build profile.
`airunner-common.LICENSE` is the wheel's GPL-3.0-only license text.

Origin
------
- Distribution: airunner-common 6.1.8
- Source repository: https://github.com/Capsize-Games/airunner-common
- Source commit: 733b0f4c8fb38952866e9cf7be2cc69793a46e92
- Wheel: airunner_common-6.1.8-py3-none-any.whl
- Wheel SHA256: ac2110ecbcd965c9a773405494bcecb3d1c6c5f127d22fde81d37478b94088fd
- File and license hashes: debian/vendor/airunner-common.json

The wheel was built from the source commit above; it was not retrieved from
PyPI. Its RECORD hashes and sizes were verified. The 13 package modules match
the source commit byte-for-byte, and the license matches both the wheel and
source LICENSE.

Why vendored
------------
airunner-common~=6.1.8 is a hard services import (235 import sites), but
Ubuntu's Python package catalog does not supply the service's pinned
dependency versions. The Debian package therefore freezes Python and its
dependencies rather than relying on dh_python3. Nothing queries airunner-common
distribution metadata at runtime (get_version() resolves airunner-services
first and falls back to package_metadata.VERSION), so no common dist-info is
required.

The common runtime package requires python-dotenv at module import time; it is
included in the CORE lock. Its legacy Shield requirement is an optional extra,
not a base dependency or an enabled runtime in this package.

Exit criteria
-------------
This source copy remains until a reviewed source or wheel update replaces it.
